#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The phase estimation problem {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"
msgstr "Le problème d'estimation de phase {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section of the lesson explains the *phase estimation problem*.\n"
"We'll begin with a short discussion of the *spectral theorem* from linear algebra, and then move on to a statement of the phase estimation problem itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cette section de la leçon explique le *problème d'estimation de phase*.\n"
"Nous commencerons par une brève discussion du *théorème spectral* de l'algèbre linéaire, puis nous passerons à l'énoncé du problème d'estimation de phase lui-même.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Spectral theorem {#spectral-theorem}"
msgstr "Théorème spectral {#spectral-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *spectral theorem* is an important fact from linear algebra that states that matrices of a certain type, called *normal matrices,* can be expressed in a simple and useful way.\n"
"We'll only need this theorem for unitary matrices in this lesson, but down the road in this series we'll apply it to Hermitian matrices as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le *théorème spectral* est un fait important de l'algèbre linéaire qui stipule que les matrices d'un certain type, appelées *matrices normales,* peuvent être exprimées d'une manière simple et utile.\n"
"Nous n'aurons besoin de ce théorème que pour les matrices unitaires dans cette leçon, mais plus loin dans cette série nous l'appliquerons également aux matrices hermitiennes.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Normal matrices {#normal-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrices normales {#normal-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $M$ with complex number entries is said to be a *normal* matrix if it commutes with its conjugate transpose:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Une matrice carrée $M$ à entrées de nombres complexes est dite matrice *normale* si elle commute avec son transposé conjugué :\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Every unitary matrix $U$ is normal because\n"
msgstr "Toute matrice unitaire $U$ est normale car\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hermitian matrices, which are matrices that equal their own conjugate transpose, are another important class of normal matrices.\n"
"If $H$ is a Hermitian matrix, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Les matrices hermitiennes, qui sont des matrices égales à leur propre transposé conjugué, sont une autre classe importante de matrices normales.\n"
"Si $H$ est une matrice hermitienne, alors\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "so $H$ is normal.\n"
msgstr "donc $H$ est normale.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every square matrix is normal.\n"
"For instance, this matrix isn't normal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Toutes les matrices carrées ne sont pas normales.\n"
"Par exemple, cette matrice n'est pas normale :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(This is a simple but great example of a matrix that's often very helpful to consider.)\n"
"It isn't normal because\n"
msgstr ""
"(C'est un exemple simple mais excellent de matrice qu'il est souvent très utile de considérer.)\n"
"Elle n'est pas normale car\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "while\n"
msgstr "tandis que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement {#theorem-statement}"
msgstr "Énoncé du théorème {#theorem-statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now here's a statement of the spectral theorem.\n"
msgstr "Voici maintenant un énoncé du théorème spectral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Let $M$ be a normal $N\\times N$ complex matrix.\n"
"There exists an orthonormal basis of $N$-dimensional complex vectors $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ along with complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Théorème\">\n"
"Théorème spectral : Soit $M$ une matrice complexe normale $N\\times N$.\n"
"Il existe une base orthonormée de vecteurs complexes à $N$ dimensions $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ ainsi que des nombres complexes $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ tels que\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The expression of a matrix in the form\n"
msgstr "L'expression d'une matrice sous la forme\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is commonly called a *spectral decomposition*.\n"
"Notice that if $M$ is a normal matrix expressed in the form $(1),$ then the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"est communément appelée *décomposition spectrale*.\n"
"Remarque : si $M$ est une matrice normale exprimée sous la forme $(1),$ alors l'équation\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"must be true for every $j = 1,\\ldots,N.$\n"
"This is a consequence of the fact that $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ is orthonormal:\n"
msgstr ""
"doit être vraie pour chaque $j = 1,\\ldots,N.$\n"
"C'est une conséquence du fait que $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ est orthonormée :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, each number $\\lambda_j$ is an *eigenvalue* of $M$ and "
"$\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* corresponding to that "
"eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Autrement dit, chaque nombre $\\lambda_j$ est une *valeur propre* de $M$ et "
"$\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ est un *vecteur propre* correspondant à cette valeur"
" propre.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 1**.\n"
"Let\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Exemple 1**.\n"
"Soit\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  which is normal.\n"
"  The theorem implies that $\\mathbb{I}$ can be written in the form $(1)$ for some choice of $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ and $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  There are multiple choices that work, including\n"
msgstr ""
"  qui est normale.\n"
"  Le théorème implique que $\\mathbb{I}$ peut être écrit sous la forme $(1)$ pour un certain choix de $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ et $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  Il existe plusieurs choix qui fonctionnent, notamment\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Notice that the theorem does not say that the complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ are\n"
"  distinct — we can have the same complex number repeated, which is necessary for this example.\n"
"  These choices work because\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Remarque : le théorème ne dit pas que les nombres complexes $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ sont\n"
"  distincts — on peut avoir le même nombre complexe répété, ce qui est nécessaire pour cet exemple.\n"
"  Ces choix fonctionnent parce que\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Indeed, we could choose $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ to be *any* orthonormal basis and the\n"
"  equation will be true. For instance,\n"
msgstr ""
"  En effet, on pourrait choisir $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ comme *n'importe quelle* base orthonormée et\n"
"  l'équation sera vraie. Par exemple,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 2**.\n"
"Consider a Hadamard operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Exemple 2**.\n"
"Considère une opération de Hadamard.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is a unitary matrix, so it is normal. The spectral theorem implies that $H$ can be written in the\n"
"  form $(1),$ and in particular we have\n"
msgstr ""
"  Il s'agit d'une matrice unitaire, donc elle est normale. Le théorème spectral implique que $H$ peut être écrit sous la\n"
"  forme $(1),$ et en particulier nous avons\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  where\n"
msgstr "  où\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  More explicitly,\n"
msgstr "  Plus explicitement,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  We can check that this decomposition is correct by performing the required"
" calculations:\n"
msgstr ""
"  On peut vérifier que cette décomposition est correcte en effectuant les "
"calculs requis :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the first example above reveals, there can be some freedom in how eigenvectors are selected.\n"
"There is, however, no freedom at all in how the eigenvalues are chosen, except for their ordering:\n"
"the same $N$ complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N,$ which can include repetitions of the same complex number, will always occur in the equation $(1)$ for a given choice of a matrix $M.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme le révèle le premier exemple ci-dessus, il peut y avoir une certaine liberté dans le choix des vecteurs propres.\n"
"Il n'y a cependant aucune liberté du tout dans le choix des valeurs propres, sauf pour leur ordonnancement :\n"
"les mêmes $N$ nombres complexes $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N,$ qui peuvent inclure des répétitions du même nombre complexe, apparaîtront toujours dans l'équation $(1)$ pour un choix donné d'une matrice $M.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's focus in on unitary matrices.\n"
"Suppose we have a complex number $\\lambda$ and a non-zero vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Concentrons-nous maintenant sur les matrices unitaires.\n"
"Supposons que nous ayons un nombre complexe $\\lambda$ et un vecteur non nul $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ satisfaisant l'équation\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $U$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an "
"eigenvector corresponding to this eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Autrement dit, $\\lambda$ est une valeur propre de $U$ et "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ est un vecteur propre correspondant à cette valeur "
"propre.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary matrices preserve Euclidean norm, and so we conclude the following "
"from $(2).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Les matrices unitaires préservent la norme euclidienne, et nous concluons "
"donc ce qui suit à partir de $(2).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The condition that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is non-zero implies that $\\bigl\\|"
" \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0,$ so we can cancel it from both sides "
"to obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"La condition que $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ est non nul implique que $\\bigl\\| "
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0,$ donc on peut l'annuler des deux côtés"
" pour obtenir\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This reveals that eigenvalues of unitary matrices must always have absolute "
"value equal to one, so they lie on the *unit circle.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela révèle que les valeurs propres des matrices unitaires doivent toujours "
"avoir une valeur absolue égale à un, donc elles se trouvent sur le *cercle "
"unité.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(The symbol $\\mathbb{T}$ is a common name for the complex unit circle. The "
"name $S^1$ is also common.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Le symbole $\\mathbb{T}$ est un nom courant pour le cercle unité complexe. "
"Le nom $S^1$ est également courant.)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Phase estimation problem statement {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"
msgstr ""
"Énoncé du problème d'estimation de phase {#phase-estimation-problem-"
"statement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the *phase estimation problem*, we're given a quantum state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ of $n$ qubits, along with a unitary quantum circuit that acts on $n$ qubits.\n"
"We're *promised* that $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of the unitary matrix $U$ that describes the action of the circuit, and our goal is to compute or approximate the eigenvalue $\\lambda$ to which $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ corresponds.\n"
"More precisely, because $\\lambda$ lies on the complex unit circle, we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans le *problème d'estimation de phase*, on nous donne un état quantique $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ de $n$ qubits, ainsi qu'un circuit quantique unitaire agissant sur $n$ qubits.\n"
"On nous *promet* que $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ est un vecteur propre de la matrice unitaire $U$ décrivant l'action du circuit, et notre objectif est de calculer ou d'approximer la valeur propre $\\lambda$ à laquelle $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ correspond.\n"
"Plus précisément, comme $\\lambda$ se trouve sur le cercle unité complexe, on peut écrire\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a unique real number $\\theta$ satisfying $0\\leq\\theta<1.$\n"
"The goal of the problem is to compute or approximate this real number $\\theta.$\n"
msgstr ""
"pour un unique nombre réel $\\theta$ satisfaisant $0\\leq\\theta<1.$\n"
"L'objectif du problème est de calculer ou d'approximer ce nombre réel $\\theta.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Phase estimation problem\">\n"
"Input: A unitary quantum circuit for an $n$-qubit operation $U$ along with an $n$-qubit quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Promise: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of $U$ \\\n"
"Output: an approximation to the number $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ satisfying $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Problème d'estimation de phase\">\n"
"Entrée : Un circuit quantique unitaire pour une opération $U$ à $n$ qubits ainsi qu'un état quantique à $n$ qubits $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Promesse : $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ est un vecteur propre de $U$ \\\n"
"Sortie : une approximation du nombre $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ satisfaisant $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few remarks about this problem statement:\n"
msgstr "Voici quelques remarques sur cet énoncé du problème :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The phase estimation problem is different from other problems we've seen so "
"far in the course in that the input includes a quantum state. Typically we "
"focus on problems having classical inputs and outputs, but nothing prevents "
"us from considering quantum state inputs like this. In terms of its "
"practical relevance, the phase estimation problem is typically encountered "
"as a *subproblem* inside of a larger computation, like we'll see in the "
"context of integer factorization later in the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le problème d'estimation de phase diffère des autres problèmes que nous "
"avons vus jusqu'à présent dans le cours en ce que l'entrée comprend un état "
"quantique. Typiquement, nous nous concentrons sur des problèmes ayant des "
"entrées et sorties classiques, mais rien ne nous empêche de considérer des "
"entrées d'état quantique comme celle-ci. En termes de pertinence pratique, "
"le problème d'estimation de phase est généralement rencontré comme un *sous-"
"problème* à l'intérieur d'un calcul plus grand, comme nous le verrons dans "
"le contexte de la factorisation d'entiers plus tard dans la leçon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The statement of the phase estimation problem above isn't specific about "
"what constitutes an approximation of $\\theta,$ but we can formulate more "
"precise problem statements depending on our needs and interests. In the "
"context of integer factorization, we'll demand a very precise approximation "
"to $\\theta,$ but in other cases we might be satisfied with a very rough "
"approximation. We'll discuss shortly how the precision we require affects "
"the computational cost of a solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"L'énoncé du problème d'estimation de phase ci-dessus n'est pas précis sur ce"
" qui constitue une approximation de $\\theta,$ mais nous pouvons formuler "
"des énoncés de problème plus précis selon nos besoins et intérêts. Dans le "
"contexte de la factorisation d'entiers, nous demanderons une approximation "
"très précise de $\\theta,$ mais dans d'autres cas une approximation très "
"grossière pourrait nous suffire. Nous discuterons bientôt de la façon dont "
"la précision que nous exigeons affecte le coût de calcul d'une solution.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that as we go from $\\theta = 0$ toward $\\theta = 1$ in the phase "
"estimation problem, we're going all the way around the unit circle, starting"
" from $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ and moving counter-clockwise toward "
"$e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1.$ That is, when we reach $\\theta = 1$ we're back "
"where we started at $\\theta = 0.$ So, as we consider the accuracy of "
"approximations, choices of $\\theta$ near $1$ should be considered as being "
"near $0.$ For example, an approximation $\\theta = 0.999$ should be "
"considered as being within $1/1000$ of $\\theta = 0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Remarque : lorsque nous allons de $\\theta = 0$ vers $\\theta = 1$ dans le "
"problème d'estimation de phase, nous faisons le tour complet du cercle "
"unité, en commençant de $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ et en nous déplaçant dans"
" le sens inverse des aiguilles d'une montre vers $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1.$"
" Autrement dit, quand nous atteignons $\\theta = 1$ nous sommes de retour où"
" nous avons commencé à $\\theta = 0.$ Donc, lorsque nous considérons la "
"précision des approximations, les valeurs de $\\theta$ proches de $1$ "
"doivent être considérées comme étant proches de $0.$ Par exemple, une "
"approximation $\\theta = 0.999$ doit être considérée comme étant à moins de "
"$1/1000$ de $\\theta = 0.$\n"
